<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarnen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarnen is the capital of the Swiss canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obwalden">Obwalden</a>, on the northern shore of Lake Sarnen. Its cantonal archive holds the White Book of Sarnen, written around 1470, which contains the earliest account of the founding of the Swiss Confederacy and the legend of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-tell">William Tell</a>. The town has long been the seat of Obwalden's government and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landsgemeinde">Landsgemeinde</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarnen.jpg" alt="Sarnen" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This file was provided to Wikimedia Commons by Roland Zumbühl of Picswiss as part of a cooperation project. If the di... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sarnen-See.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
